{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observed signal\nError sweep window 2026-08-30T21:20:00-07:00..2026-09-01T11:58:00-07:00 (2026-08-31T04:20:00Z..2026-09-01T18:58:00Z) found GitHub Actions run 33455923923 (`Jira DC Exact-Patchset Parity`, workflow_dispatch, triggered by JoeOakhartNava) failed before executing the live DC parity body.\n\nFailing job: `jira DC exact-patchset parity (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)` at step `Verify the checkout landed on the exact patchset SHA`.\n\nError:\n`checked-out HEAD (d6c37680805fc8ae013832dd4c09c1fb100a1e0b) does not match the requested Gerrit patchset revision (a22257e7d10e3d079ee676cbb38d2b39811d0fd5) — refusing to run the DC lane against the wrong ref.`\n\n## Confirmed root cause\nGerrit change 2466 patchset 1 (`refs/changes/66/2466/1`) resolves to `d6c37680805fc8ae013832dd4c09c1fb100a1e0b`; patchset 2/current resolves to `a22257e7d10e3d079ee676cbb38d2b39811d0fd5`. Run 33455923923 combined the patchset-1 refspec with the patchset-2 revision. The pinned `checkout-gerrit-change-action` first checks out its `ref` default (`github.sha`) but then fetches `GERRIT_REFSPEC` and unconditionally checks out `FETCH_HEAD`, so the workflow landed on the stale refspec commit and only the later guard detected the mismatch.\n\nThe guard's fail-closed behavior is correct. The defect is that `.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml` delegates the final checkout to a refspec-first third-party action even though this lane's authoritative requested commit is `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION`.\n\n## Fix plan\nReplace only this workflow's first step with two explicit, narrow steps:\n\n1. Use the already-approved, SHA-pinned `actions/checkout` action to check out `ref: ${{ inputs.GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION }}` with `fetch-depth: 1`. This makes the final working tree target the requested SHA, not whatever commit `GERRIT_REFSPEC` names.\n2. Run a shell validation step that fetches `GERRIT_REFSPEC` into `FETCH_HEAD` without checking it out. It fetches from the existing `origin` remote created by `actions/checkout` (the GitHub mirror, with the workflow token/auth setup already handled by `actions/checkout`) and falls back to anonymous HTTPS `https://${{ vars.GERRIT_SERVER }}/${{ inputs.GERRIT_PROJECT }}`, matching the checkout action's existing Gerrit fallback surface.\n3. Compare `FETCH_HEAD^{commit}` to `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION`; if they differ, fail with a clear dispatch-input error naming the refspec SHA and expected SHA, while the workspace remains at the requested SHA.\n4. Keep the existing `git rev-parse HEAD` guard immediately after validation so no Python/Jira DC setup or live DC operation runs unless `HEAD == GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION`.\n\nStrengthen `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py` by replacing the old `test_uses_pinned_gerrit_checkout_action` assertion with contract tests for the new shape: the workflow must use pinned `actions/checkout` at `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION`, must not use the refspec-first third-party checkout action in this lane, and its validation shell must fail on an inconsistent temporary-git refspec/revision pair without checking out the refspec commit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The Jira DC exact-patchset parity workflow checks out the exact requested Gerrit patchset SHA before any live DC operation runs; checked by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py -q` and by the existing `HEAD == GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` guard embedded in the workflow.\n- [ ] If the requested patchset refspec cannot be fetched from either the GitHub mirror or Gerrit fallback, the workflow fails with a clear fetch/input error rather than landing on a different commit; checked by a focused temporary-git test in `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py`.\n- [ ] The workflow records enough evidence for a future CI dispatch to prove the live Data Center lane ran from `HEAD == expected_sha`; in-session completion rests on AC1/AC2 plus Gerrit review/Verified results, and the future live dispatch evidence is a GitHub Actions run id whose summary lists the verified SHA.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions workflow_dispatch with real Jira Data Center image; principal=Gerrit/GitHub workflow actor; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — the real Jira DC Docker image only runs in CI, so this session proves the checkout/verify plumbing locally and relies on Gerrit `Verified` plus a future explicit dispatch for the live DC body.\n\n## Testing\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`\n\nDo not run the real Jira DC parity body locally; the operator confirmed the real Data Center Docker image used by this lane only runs in CI."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788315723722195900,"uuid":"fe6825dd-f22c-47ef-bb19-4cf348cd9b35"}